==============================================================================
  observed residual DiD (ts_gsr W60, primary) = +0.01153  95 % CI [+0.00181, +0.02111]
  sign-flip p against 0                        = 0.0422
  null = +0.0054 (primary null (h = 0.5, DMT-post/placebo ACF)):
      inside the observed 95 % CI? YES;  sign-flip p for (observed - null) = 0.2506
  null = +0.0037 (lowest of the third review's variations):
      inside the observed 95 % CI? YES;  sign-flip p for (observed - null) = 0.1500
  null = +0.0077 (highest of the third review's variations):
      inside the observed 95 % CI? YES;  sign-flip p for (observed - null) = 0.4661
  null = +0.0052 (third review, h = 0.5):
      inside the observed 95 % CI? YES;  sign-flip p for (observed - null) = 0.2378
  null = +0.0059 (third review, h = 0.25):
      inside the observed 95 % CI? YES;  sign-flip p for (observed - null) = 0.2903
  => EVERY null value, including the largest, lies inside the observed CI, and the
     excess over the null is not significant at any of them.  The residual DiD is
     statistically compatible with being entirely finite-sample under this null.

